@@ -0,0 +1,1294 @@
+# SGP ESE5004 Stage2
+# Phase 4 — Full-SC Research Model Assembly & Validation
+# Gate 4 — First Full-SC Research Network Assembly
+#
+# GOAL:
+# Build the first complete, UNSOLVED ASEAN sector-coupled Research Network.
+# This is NOT yet a formal experiment and MUST NOT run an optimizer.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+0. Authoritative starting state
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+Research branch:
+
+research/full-sc-baseline
+
+Gate3 accepted Research HEAD:
+
+fa82156ee74a1fd2a93a88b774c9f9827c2d3f4c
+
+Before any change verify:
+
+git branch --show-current
+git status
+git rev-parse HEAD
+git log -1
+
+Required:
+
+branch = research/full-sc-baseline
+
+HEAD =
+fa82156ee74a1fd2a93a88b774c9f9827c2d3f4c
+
+working tree = CLEAN
+
+Remote main must remain unchanged.
+
+If the Research HEAD differs unexpectedly:
+
+STOP.
+
+Do not attempt to reconstruct history from memory.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+1. Gate4 objective
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+Gate4 has THREE engineering steps:
+
+A. Assembly Input Freeze
+
+B. Topology Repair + Full Research Network Build
+
+C. Actual-Network Static Validation
+
+At the end we want:
+
+one complete unsolved Research Full-SC network
+
+with:
+
+- real Research demand ownership;
+- Research carrier architecture;
+- Research carbon architecture;
+- valid topology;
+- no silent missing-to-zero behaviour;
+- no unintended cross-border carrier sharing;
+- identifiable active sector-coupling pathways;
+- an exact future cross-border electricity control set.
+
+DO NOT run an optimizer.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+2. Important scope rule
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+Do NOT reopen Phase1–3 sector design.
+
+Already frozen:
+
+Buildings:
+minimum-defensible / mostly embedded
+
+Transport:
+aggregate road + explicit EV structure;
+rail embedded;
+shipping/aviation fixed fuel obligations
+
+Industry:
+fixed final-energy core + qualified substitution only
+
+Agriculture:
+embedded/fixed
+
+Cross-border electricity:
+future core intervention
+
+Cross-border H2:
+OFF
+
+Cross-border gas physical network:
+OFF
+
+Cross-border CO2:
+OFF
+
+NH3/methanol networks:
+OFF/deferred
+
+PolicyCO2_Power:
+separate from ReportingCO2_FullSystem
+
+Do not redesign these unless the assembly proves an actual contradiction.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+3. Gate4 philosophy — Minimum Defensible Assembly
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+This Gate must NOT become another broad data-search phase.
+
+Use:
+
+major-system correctness
+>
+minor-detail completeness
+
+For an unresolved detail ask:
+
+“Can this credibly change system cost, major capacity,
+sector electrification, H2/synthetic-fuel demand,
+cross-border electricity flows, or Integrated-vs-Disconnected value?”
+
+If NO:
+
+document limitation and proceed.
+
+If YES:
+
+treat as assembly blocker.
+
+Do not invent a numeric materiality threshold.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+4. Step A — Assembly Input Freeze
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+Gate2 created the demand ledger and many numerical candidates remain PENDING.
+
+Gate4 must create the minimum defensible numerical input set needed to build the first Research network.
+
+Do NOT broadly search for new datasets.
+
+Priority:
+
+1. existing Human-frozen decisions;
+2. authoritative source values already recovered;
+3. validated frozen upstream values when scientifically compatible;
+4. transparent embedded/fixed fallback;
+5. if material source conflict remains, STOP that account rather than guessing.
+
+--------------------------------------------------
+5. Numeric acceptance rule
+--------------------------------------------------
+
+Codex must NOT silently mark arbitrary candidates HUMAN_ACCEPTED.
+
+Create an explicit Gate4 assembly status:
+
+ASSEMBLY_V1_ACCEPTED
+
